ECT_SUMMARY, SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY, SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION, ACADEMIC_TERMS, TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED, STUDENT_DEPARTMENT — `semantic_get` ✔\n- dw_1350, dw_4387, dw_3868, dw_2151, dw_1335, dw_4812, dw_2924, dw_3163, dw_2272 — `semantic_get` (full SQL) ✔\n- column_concept_total_units, column_concept_enrollment_measures — `semantic_get` ✔\n- Remaining Phase-1 entities (facilities/space/IAP/Moira/time-dimension families, HR org tables, CIP, library/TIP detail tables, etc.) are unrelated to units/enrollment stats and were discarded per screening criteria.\n- `mysql_query` — attempted 8+ times; **all failed with server error 1045 \"Access denied for user 'root'@'localhost'\"** (infrastructure-level authentication failure, not a SQL issue). Execution verification was therefore impossible.\n\n### 6. Recommendation\n\n**6a.** Part 1 (UnitsStats): `SIS_DEPARTMENT` (IS_DEGREE_GRANTING='Y', DEPARTMENT_CODE<>'18', SCHOOL_NAME/DEPARTMENT_NAME) joined to `COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED` (ACADEMIC_YEAR=2022, TOTAL_UNITS) — per dw_2151; department-level stats UNION ALL school-level rollup with NULL department name — per dw_1350. Part 2 (EnrollmentStats): `SIS_DEPARTMENT` + `TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED` + `STUDENT_DEPARTMENT` — per dw_4387/dw_3868 — with HAVING SUM(NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS)>50, IS_DEGREE_GRANTING='Y', DEPARTMENT_NAME<>'Management'; most popular course via ROW_NUMBER over TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED ordered by NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS DESC — per dw_4812. Reason literals and NULL-padding per dw_1335.\n\n**6b/6c.** Two-level aggregation not required (single grouping level per branch); VARIANCE() and MAX−MIN for range; no rounding. Data perspective: ACADEMIC_YEAR physically exists only on the catalog table (column defs); TIP enrollment is the documented department-total source (column_concept_enrollment_measures decision guide). Semantic-network perspective: exact-shape precedents cited above. Business perspective: wording of this task is nearly verbatim to dw_2151 + dw_4387 + dw_1350 + dw_1335.